title: "How much of a nervous-system model does behaviour identify?"
authors:
  - family-names: He
    given-names: Chenxi
    affiliation: "Cavendish Laboratory, University of Cambridge"
    email: ch2067@cam.ac.uk
version: "1.4.1"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22120856"
date-released: "2026-08-27"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - behavioural-equivalence manifold
  - identifiability
  - sloppy models
  - neural degeneracy
  - whole-organism simulation
  - Caenorhabditis elegans
abstract: >-
  Code, result files and reproduction container for a study measuring how much of a whole-organism
  nervous-system model behaviour constrains. One Gauss-Newton curvature estimator is applied to
  every system, each reported dimension is gated on observable count, linearity and noise floor,
  and ground truth from eleven cell models separates behavioural fit quality from parameter
  recovery.
